@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.435 = private unnamed_addr constant [602 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for calls to trio functions that are not immediately awaited.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AMany of the functions exposed by trio are asynchronous, and must be awaited\0Ato take effect. Calling a trio function without an `await` can lead to\0A`RuntimeWarning` diagnostics and unexpected behaviour.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aasync def double_sleep(x):\0A    trio.sleep(2 * x)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aasync def double_sleep(x):\0A    await trio.sleep(2 * x)\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe, as adding an `await` to a function\0Acall changes its semantics and runtime behavior.\0A", align 1
