@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.442 = private unnamed_addr constant [629 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for files with overly permissive permissions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AOverly permissive file permissions may allow unintended access and\0Aarbitrary code execution.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport os\0A\0Aos.chmod(\22/etc/secrets.txt\22, 0o666)  # rw-rw-rw-\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport os\0A\0Aos.chmod(\22/etc/secrets.txt\22, 0o600)  # rw-------\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `os.chmod`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.html#os.chmod)\0A- [Python documentation: `stat`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stat.html)\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-732](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/732.html)\0A", align 1
