@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.542 = private unnamed_addr constant [998 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for functions names that do not follow the `snake_case` naming\0Aconvention.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 8] recommends that function names follow `snake_case`:\0A\0A> Function names should be lowercase, with words separated by underscores as necessary to\0A> improve readability. mixedCase is allowed only in contexts where that\E2\80\99s already the\0A> prevailing style (e.g. threading.py), to retain backwards compatibility.\0A\0ANames can be excluded from this rule using the [`lint.pep8-naming.ignore-names`]\0Aor [`lint.pep8-naming.extend-ignore-names`] configuration options. For example,\0Ato ignore all functions starting with `test_` from this rule, set the\0A[`lint.pep8-naming.extend-ignore-names`] option to `[\22test_*\22]`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef myFunction():\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef my_function():\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.ignore-names`\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.extend-ignore-names`\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#function-and-variable-names\0A", align 1
