@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.589 = private unnamed_addr constant [614 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for over-indented code.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAccording to [PEP 8], 4 spaces per indentation level should be preferred. Increased\0Aindentation can lead to inconsistent formatting, which can hurt\0Areadability.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afor item in items:\0A      pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afor item in items:\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0A## Formatter compatibility\0AWe recommend against using this rule alongside the [formatter]. The\0Aformatter enforces consistent indentation, making the rule redundant.\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#indentation\0A[formatter]:https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter/\0A", align 1
